The H3 C library is vendored, unmodified, under native/h3lib, and the iOS static
libraries and cinterop header under src/iosMain/cinterop are built from it. Those
files retain Uber's copyright notices in their headers. The upstream release tag
and commit are recorded in native/PROVENANCE. The static libraries are embedded
in this library's published iOS artifacts, so this NOTICE and the LICENSE are
included in every published jar under META-INF.

src/commonTest/kotlin/UberH3Fixtures.kt is derived from H3's own test input
files (tests/inputfiles) at that same release, and is used only by this
library's tests. It is modified: a subset of the rows is selected and reformatted
into Kotlin source by native/generate-agreement-fixtures.py.

The JVM target depends on com.uber:h3, the Android target on com.uber:h3-android
(both from https://github.com/uber/h3-java), and the JS and wasmJs targets on the
h3-js package. None of them is redistributed here.

